  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on preferring the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome, which in this case is Lottery B (100% vs 80%). The individual considers the same information — the 80% vs 100% chance of receiving a positive amount — and explicitly references the 20% risk of zero as a decisive factor. Their justification aligns with the rule of the decision reason: favoring the option with higher probability of a favorable (i.e., non-zero) outcome. Although the individual does not phrase it in abstract rule-based terms, their reasoning directly mirrors the core logic of the decision reason. The emphasis on the certainty of gain and aversion to the risk of nothing indicates a clear application of probability-based preference for more certain positive outcomes.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
